+++ b/docs/install.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Install Hive
+
+Hive releases are self-contained binaries: you do not need system Ruby.
+
+On macOS arm64, Ubuntu 22.04+ x86_64, or Arch Linux x86_64, install the latest
+stable release into `~/.local/bin`:
+
+```bash
+curl -fsSL https://github.com/ivankuznetsov/hive/releases/latest/download/install.sh | bash
+```
+
+Set `HIVE_VERSION=v0.1.0` to pin an immutable stable release. The installer
+downloads the release manifest and binary, verifies SHA-256 before moving it
+into place, and writes an XDG state receipt. It never installs `git`, agent
+CLIs, `gh`, or `jq`; it reports any missing tools with a next step instead.
+
+If another program owns `hive`, the installer leaves it untouched and installs
+Hive as `hv`. It does not edit shell profiles; add `~/.local/bin` to your PATH
+yourself if needed. Verify with `hive --version` (or `hv --version`), then run
+`hive init` when you are ready to attach a project.
